    "q-95209": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95209",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the dimension of ${R}_{12}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $12?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{12}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{12}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{12}[t])=12+1=13.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$",
