      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the dimension of ${R}_{4}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $4?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,\\,{t}^{n}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{4}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{4}[t])=5.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
