    "q-106888": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106888",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "What is the dimension of ${\\text{M}}_{8}(R),$ the vector space of all $8\\times 8$ matrices over $R?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{n}(R)$ contains a total of ${n}^{2}$ matrices, each with one nonzero entry that is equal to $1.$ \n\nFor example, the standard basis of ${\\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ contains ${2}^{2}=4$ elements, and is given by\n\n$$\n\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for ${\\text{M}}_{8}(R),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{8}(R))={8}^{2}=64.\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
