    "q-106899": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106899",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $7?$\n\nI. ${\\text{M}}_{7}(R),$ the vector space of all $7\\times 7$ matrices over $R$\n\nII. ${R}^{7}$\n\nIII. ${R}_{7}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $7$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n}(R))={n}^{2}.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{7}(R))={7}^{2}=49\\ne 7.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{7})=7.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{7}[t])=7+1=8.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
