    "q-106901": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106901",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $20?$\n\nI. ${R}_{20}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $20$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{4\\times 5}(R),$ the vector space of all $4\\times 5$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}^{20}$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{20}[t])=20+1=21\\ne 20.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{4\\times 5}(R))=4\\cdot 5=20.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{20})=20.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
