    "q-106904": {
      "dom_id": "step-q106904",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Which of the following vector spaces has a dimension of $11?$\n\nI. ${R}_{10}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $10$\n\nII. ${\\text{M}}_{2\\times 6}(R),$ the vector space of all $2\\times 6$ matrices over $R$\n\nIII. ${R}^{10}$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the vector spaces in turn.\n\nI. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}_{10}[t])=10+1=11.\\,✓\n  $$\n\nII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{n\\times m}(R))=n\\cdot m.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{2\\times 6}(R))=2\\cdot 6=12\\ne 11.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nIII. Recall that $\\text{dim}({R}^{n})=n.$ Therefore, \n\n  $$\n  \\text{dim}({R}^{10})=10\\ne 11.\\,\\times \n  $$\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
